const faqItems = [
  {
    q: 'What is the best postgraduate course for science students in India?',
    a: 'There is no single best course; the right one depends on your subject and your goals. A Maths or Statistics background points most strongly toward actuarial science or data science, a Physics or Chemistry background points toward CSIR-NET JRF and a PhD if you want research, and a Biology or Biotechnology background points toward clinical research or regulatory affairs if you want faster industry entry. Compare the route, not just the subject, before deciding.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Should I do MSc or go straight for a PhD after a science degree?',
    a: 'Most Indian PhD programs, including the Integrated PhD tracks at IISc, TIFR, and the IISERs, admit directly from a bachelor\'s degree through exams like JEST, so MSc is not always a required step. If you are not certain you want a 4-6 year research commitment, an MSc first gives you two more years to test that fit before locking in a PhD, at the cost of a longer overall timeline.',
  },
