        </div>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

  <h2 id="gates">Pass The 3 Gates before you spend money or years</h2>

  <p>
    The 4-Checkpoint Protocol above helps you compare routes on paper.
  </p>

  <p>
    The 3 Gates make you test the route in the real world before you commit an entrance-exam preparation
    year or several years of postgraduate study to it.
  </p>

  <div class="gates-block">
    <p class="gates-block__title">
      Do not lock in a multi-year plan, a PhD registration, or an education loan before passing all three
      gates.
    </p>
    <div class="gates-row">
      {gateItems.map((item) => (
        <div class="gate">
          <span class="gate__num">{item.num}</span>
          <span class="gate__name">{item.title}</span>
          <p>{item.body}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="highlight-box highlight-box--teal">
    <p>
      <strong>A high-value skill portfolio after a postgraduate route is never just the subject expertise
      in isolation.</strong> It is the right route mix for you specifically, real proof of that work, a
      published paper, a shipped project, a cleared exam tier, the ability to explain it clearly to a
      hiring panel or an admissions committee, where you sit against everyone else chasing the same
      fellowship or role, and whether the plan actually fits your family's financial reality. A
      postgraduate route that produces only a degree certificate and no proof of work moves you toward
      <strong>earlier financial freedom</strong> far more slowly than one that produces a real result
      alongside it.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p>
    If you are still not sure which lane genuinely fits your subject, a session inside
    <a href="https://futurecareerschool.com/services/career-counselling-and-career-guidance/">career guidance</a>
    can help you run this comparison with an actual person instead of guessing alone or copying a senior's
    path that may not fit your subject or your finances.
  </p>

